 "post": {
  "title": "Try This 12-Word Memory Test (Your Brain Skips the Middle) #shorts",
  "description": "The serial-position effect: in 1962 Bennet Murdock had people study lists of words and recall them in any order. Recall made a U-shaped curve: the first words (primacy) and the last words (recency) were remembered best, the middle worst. Early words get more rehearsal; the last ones are still in short-term memory. Put your key point first or last. Murdock, B. B., Jr. (1962). The serial position effect of free recall. Journal of Experimental Psychology, 64(5), 482-488. #psychology #shorts #memory #serialposition",
  "tags": [
   "serial position effect",
   "psychology",
   "memory",
   "primacy effect",
   "recency effect"
  ]
 },
